{% set guidance %}
This is progressive analog-evidence reasoning. Decide the exact task endpoint,
not generic permeability, exposure, toxicity, or computational plausibility.

Reason in two stages. First infer the experimental outcome direction within
each reference parent-condition context. Treat all records from one context as
one body of evidence, not as independent votes. At L2, revise that context only
when the added records clarify or contradict its L1 interpretation; never count
L2 cards as new gold votes.

Second judge how well each context applies to the query, then compare the
weighted balance of supportive and contradictory contexts. Treat
morgan_similarity as radius-2, 2048-bit fingerprint Tanimoto structural
proximity, not as a label probability, experimental result, or guarantee of
biological transferability. A concrete endpoint, assay, species, formulation,
exposure, condition, or structural mismatch can outweigh it. Do not use a
universal similarity cutoff.

Apply symmetric evidentiary standards. A valid direct positive outcome supports
the positive class and a valid direct negative outcome supports the negative
class; neither requires an additional speculative mechanism. Missing,
ambiguous, indirect, or nontransferable evidence is neutral rather than evidence
for either class. Use the query physicochemical prior only as a tie-breaker when
the applicable experimental evidence is genuinely balanced or sparse.

{% if task == "bioavailability_ma" %}
The decision is absolute oral bioavailability F >= 20% versus F < 20%. Prefer
measured absolute or relative bioavailability and matched oral-versus-reference
exposure. Interpret dose, route, formulation, species, AUC, Cmax, sampling, and
reference context together. An adequately matched measured F < 20% outcome is
affirmative negative evidence; an adequately matched F >= 20% outcome is
affirmative positive evidence. Permeability, solubility, exposure, metabolism,
or transporter mechanisms alone are indirect and cannot define the label.
{% elif task == "skin_reaction" %}
The decision is skin sensitization or contact allergy versus no sensitization.
Prefer validated human or in vivo sensitization outcomes and accepted integrated
outcomes. An adequately exposed validated negative sensitization result is
affirmative no-risk evidence; a validated positive result is affirmative risk
evidence. AOP key events may modify confidence when coherent and applicable,
but irritation, corrosion, phototoxicity, generic injury, permeability, or one
mechanistic event alone cannot define the label.
{% elif task == "bbb_martins" %}
The decision is meaningful CNS access. Prefer direct in vivo brain or unbound-
brain exposure, brain-to-systemic ratios, CNS biodistribution, PET, and
autoradiography. Treat CSF as a qualified proxy. Generic permeability, efflux,
or another mechanism alone cannot prove or disprove meaningful CNS access.
{% endif %}

Ground every compound-specific empirical claim in cited record cards. Return
exactly one valid JSON object and do not reveal hidden chain-of-thought.
{% endset %}
[
  {
    "role": "system",
    "content": {{ (system_role ~ "\n\n" ~ (guidance | trim)) | tojson }}
  },
  {
    "role": "user",
    "content": {{ user_content | tojson }}
  }
]
